{
  "dom_id": "step-q118000",
  "name": "Question 8",
  "problem": "The surface area of a cylinder is $24\\pi \\,{\\text{mm}}^{2}$ and the ratio of its radius to its height is $3.$ Calculate the height of the cylinder.",
  "worked_solution": "Let $r$ and $h$ be the radius and height of the cylinder, respectively. \n\nWe are given that \n\n$$\n\\frac{r}{h}=3\\,⟹\\,r=3h.\n$$\n\nWe can find the surface area of a cylinder using the formula\n\n$$\nS=2\\pi {r}^{2}+2\\pi rh.\n$$\n\nSubstituting the values\n\n$$\nS=24\\pi ,\\,r=3h\n$$\n\ninto the formula for $S,$ we obtain the following:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}S & =2\\pi {r}^{2}+2\\pi rh \\\\ 24\\pi  & =2\\pi (3h)^{2}+2\\pi (3h)h \\\\ 24\\pi  & =18\\pi {h}^{2}+6\\pi {h}^{2} \\\\ 24\\pi  & =24\\pi {h}^{2} \\\\ {h}^{2} & =\\frac{24\\pi }{24\\pi } \\\\ {h}^{2} & =1 \\\\ h & =1\\,\\text{mm}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNotice that we disregard the negative solution since length must be positive.",
  "calculator_instructions": "",
